page('cover-studies.html','Cover studies',head('The fragrance of earth. The voice of the heart.','A different world<br>on every cover.','Realistic, artistic cover imagery gives each issue its own presence. Quiet interior pages keep the reading experience consistent.')+covercards()+'<div class="notice">Three new generated photographic studies demonstrate the direction. They are proposed treatments, not original historical covers or final approved issue art. The images carry no generated lettering: the magazine name and issue details are typeset separately.</div><div class="three"><div><h2>Earth after rain</h2><p class="small">An Odisha-inspired monsoon study: rain-dark earth and a fallen flower. A future location photograph should name its place and maker.</p></div><div><h2>Window & memory</h2><p class="small">A lived-in home: a clay cup, worn wood and rain light. Commission a real Odisha courtyard or window as a future companion.</p></div><div><h2>Evening water</h2><p class="small">A visual direction for Chilika’s quiet wetland edges: water, reeds and an empty boat. This generated study is not a photograph of Chilika.</p></div></div>',desc='Three realistic photographic cover studies with an English masthead and separate Odia signature.')
